# Python Standards

## Tooling

- Python 3.12+, config in `pyproject.toml` (Ruff line-length 120, Mypy strict)
- Run `make format && make lint` before PRs
- Use `from __future__ import annotations` in new modules

## Naming

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Modules | snake_case | `state_machine.py` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `IngestionRepository` |
| Functions | snake_case | `persist_canonical_logs` |
| Private helpers | `_leading_underscore` | `_map_geotab_status` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `COMPLIANCE_ALERTS_CHANNEL` |
| ORM models | PascalCase + `Record` suffix | `CanonicalHOSLogRecord` |
| API responses | `*Response` suffix | `ComplianceSnapshotResponse` |
| Canonical model | `DCW` prefix | `DCWCanonicalHOSLog` |

## Logging

```python
logger = logging.getLogger("dcw.<domain>.<component>")
# e.g. dcw.ingestion.poller, dcw.engine.rule_pack, dcw.adapters.geotab
```

## Immutability & Time

- Use `model_config = ConfigDict(frozen=True)` for canonical and compliance types
- All datetimes must be UTC-aware (`timezone.utc` / `zoneinfo`)
- Tenant scope: always filter by `tenant_id` on queries

## Redis Key Patterns

```
cursor:{provider}:{tenant_id}
set:active_drivers
alert_lock:{tenant_id}:{driver_id}:{shift_id}:{rule}:{stage}
```
